# 102. Navigation Configuration

Recommended conceptual model:

```text
NavigationConfig
├── role
├── sections
│   ├── label
│   └── items
│       ├── label
│       ├── icon
│       ├── route
│       ├── activeMatch
│       └── capability
```

Backend authorization remains authoritative.

---

# 103. Capability-Aware Navigation

If backend/application exposes capabilities, navigation may use them to improve UX.

Example:

```text
canViewProjectDefinitions
canViewAdminAnalytics
```

Capabilities are UX inputs, not security guarantees.

---

# 104. Shell Context

A shell context/provider may expose:

```text
currentUser
currentWorkspace
authorizedWorkspaces
sidebarState
theme
notificationSummary
searchState
```

Keep the context focused.

Do not turn it into a universal application store.

---

# 105. Shell Events

Possible shell events:

```text
WORKSPACE_CHANGED
NOTIFICATION_RECEIVED
NOTIFICATION_READ
SEARCH_OPENED
SEARCH_CLOSED
SIDEBAR_COLLAPSED
SIDEBAR_EXPANDED
THEME_CHANGED
SESSION_EXPIRED
```

Events should represent UI/application behavior, not replace canonical domain events.

---

# 106. Shell Analytics

Shell observability may measure:

- navigation usage
- search usage
- workspace switching
- sidebar interactions
- notification interactions
- shell rendering performance
- navigation errors

Do not collect unnecessary personal data.

---

# 107. Performance

Shell should be lightweight because it exists on almost every page.

Requirements:

- minimize initial bundle impact
- lazy-load heavy search interfaces
- lazy-load large notification previews where appropriate
- avoid expensive global rerenders
- avoid unnecessary providers
- keep icons optimized
- keep shell transitions lightweight

---

# 108. Shell Rendering Strategy

The shell should remain mounted across normal authenticated route transitions where architecture permits.

Benefits:

- navigation remains stable
- sidebar state persists
- fewer visual jumps
- better perceived performance

---

# 109. Route Transition Strategy

For normal navigation:

```text
Route change
 ↓
Keep shell
 ↓
Load page/feature
 ↓
Render local loading state
 ↓
Render page
```

Avoid full shell reconstruction on every route.

---

# 110. Code Splitting

Potential split boundaries:

```text
public
auth
student
mentor
admin
heavy charts
AI interface
document editor/viewer
```

The shell should not eagerly load every role-specific feature.

---

# 111. Role Bundle Isolation

A BUILD user should not unnecessarily download all GOVERN administrative functionality merely because the shell supports it.

Where practical:

```text
shared shell
+
role-specific code
```

---

# 112. Search Loading

Search UI may be lazy-loaded because it can contain:

- command palette logic
- indexing/search rendering
- result previews

The trigger itself should remain lightweight.

---

# 113. Notification Loading

Notification preview should remain efficient.

Do not load an entire notification center implementation merely to display an unread count.

